At the 16 residual stops under PF3+C5, the end-of-turn logprob is -0.0 to -3.4 (median about -1.6). The layer-13 pair is active just before (0.2 to 0.8). In thinking-repeat positions (loops E, rewritten drafts L) the pair adds only about 0.15 to 0.19 (13/16) and 0.07 to 0.13 (13/7). So the loop exit in thinking relies mainly on the layer-10 and layer-14 detectors, while the residual answer drive is mostly the layer-13 pair. That makes an answer-phase-specific suppression of 13/16 and 13/7 attractive.

I'll load the answer-phase direction d13 (fit earlier on start activations). Then I'll check that it still separates the phases on the exact PF3+C5 inputs: answer about 1, thinking about 0, including the new N texts not used to fit it. I'll also compute the gate and up pre-activations of both neurons by region.

```python
# Check answer-phase direction d13 on PF3C5 inputs (incl. new N texts not used to fit it); z_g, z_u of 13/16, 13/7 by region
AD = np.load('/work/answer_dirs_v1.npz'); d13 = AD['d13'].astype(np.float32); print('d13 norm', np.linalg.norm(d13))
Xc = {}; P = {}; ZG = {}; ZU = {}
for i in range(63):
    X = x13(i); Xc[i] = X.astype(np.float16)
    P[i] = X @ d13; ZG[i] = X @ Wg13[[16,7]].T; ZU[i] = X @ Wu13[[16,7]].T
def rstat(gname, key, f):
    idx = [i for i in range(63) if grp[i]==gname]
    v = np.concatenate([f(i)[REG[i][key]] for i in idx]) if idx else np.array([np.nan])
    return v
for gname in ['A','N','B','C','D','E','L']:
    out = [gname]
    for key in ['think','trep','ans','copy']:
        v = rstat(gname, key, lambda i: P[i])
        out.append('%s p %.2f[%.2f,%.2f]' % (key, np.median(v), np.percentile(v,5), np.percentile(v,95)) if len(v)>1 else key+' -')
    print(' | '.join(out))
for gname in ['A','N','E','L','B','C']:
    for key in (['copy','trep'] if gname in 'AN' else ['trep','ans']):
        v1 = rstat(gname, key, lambda i: ZG[i][:,0]); v2 = rstat(gname, key, lambda i: ZU[i][:,0]); v3 = rstat(gname, key, lambda i: ZG[i][:,1]); v4 = rstat(gname, key, lambda i: ZU[i][:,1])
        if len(v1)>1: print(gname, key, 'n16 zg %.2f zu %.2f | n7 zg %.2f zu %.2f' % (np.median(v1), np.median(v2), np.median(v3), np.median(v4)))
```

P13 is back. I'll compare PF5C5 (P13) with PF3+C5 (P12, identical tokens) and, for the first 38 texts, with start (P2). The comparison covers:
- whether the layer-13 edit is realized and how 14/239 reacts;
- the end-of-turn logprob at the early stop points of A and N;
- the expected premature stops in answers;
- natural ends of B/C/D;
- loop exits (`</think>` mass in E) and end-of-turn leaks in thinking;
- per-token changes in thinking and in copied answer text.

```python
# P13 (PF5C5) vs P12 (PF3C5) vs P2 (start): stop points, natural ends, loop exit, leaks, token dlp, realized acts
T13 = np.load('/work/fwd_13/tokens.npy'); LP13 = np.load('/work/fwd_13/token_logprobs.npy')
TKI13 = np.load('/work/fwd_13/topk_ids.npy', mmap_mode='r'); TKL13 = np.load('/work/fwd_13/topk_logprobs.npy', mmap_mode='r')
TKI12 = np.load('/work/fwd_12/topk_ids.npy', mmap_mode='r'); TKL12 = np.load('/work/fwd_12/topk_logprobs.npy', mmap_mode='r')
MA13 = np.load('/work/fwd_13/mlp_act.npy', mmap_mode='r')
print('tokens equal', np.array_equal(T13, T12), '| P2 tokens match first 38:', np.array_equal(np.asarray(T2)[:38,:min(T2.shape[1],T12.shape[1])][:, :100], T12[:38,:100]))
def pnx(TKI, TKL, i, tid):
    n = lens12[i]; ids_ = TKI[i,:n]; lps = TKL[i,:n]
    return np.where(ids_ == tid, np.exp(lps), 0).sum(1)
def final_lp(LPx, i): n = lens12[i]; return LPx[i, n-1] if T12[i,n-1] == IM else np.nan
res = defaultdict(dict)
for nm_, (LPx, TKI, TKL) in {'PF3C5': (LP12, TKI12, TKL12), 'PF5C5': (LP13, TKI13, TKL13)}.items():
    for gl in 'ANBCDEL':
        idx = [i for i in range(63) if grp[i]==gl]
        fl = [final_lp(LPx, i) for i in idx]
        pim = [pnx(TKI, TKL, i, IM) for i in idx]; pth = [pnx(TKI, TKL, i, ETH) for i in idx]
        prem = [ (pim[k][REG[i]['ans']][:-2]).sum() if REG[i]['ans'].any() else np.nan for k,i in enumerate(idx)]
        leak = [ (pim[k][REG[i]['think']]).sum() for k,i in enumerate(idx)]
        ethm = [ (pth[k][REG[i]['think']]).sum() for k,i in enumerate(idx)]
        res[gl][nm_] = dict(final=np.nanmedian(fl), prem=np.nanmean(prem), leak=np.mean(leak), think_eth=np.mean(ethm))
for gl in 'ANBCDEL':
    print(gl, {k: {kk: round(float(vv),3) for kk,vv in v.items()} for k,v in res[gl].items()})
dth = np.concatenate([(LP13[i]-LP12[i])[REG[i]['think']] for i in range(63)]); dcp = np.concatenate([(LP13[i]-LP12[i])[REG[i]['copy']] for i in range(63) if grp[i] in 'AN'])
dans = {gl: np.concatenate([(LP13[i]-LP12[i])[REG[i]['ans']][:-1] for i in range(63) if grp[i]==gl]) for gl in 'BCD'}
print('dlp PF5-PF3: think %.4f | copy %.4f | ans B %.4f C %.4f D %.4f' % (np.nanmean(dth), np.nanmean(dcp), *[np.nanmean(dans[g]) for g in 'BCD']))
```

